An analysis of Virginia Power’s results of operations follows:
Third Quarter 2026 vs. 2025
Operating revenue increased 27%, primarily reflecting:
•A $348 million net increase in fuel-related revenue as a result of an increase in commodity costs associated with sales to electric utility retail customers, including revenue for the deferred fuel securitization and electric utility customers who elect to pay market based or other negotiated rates and related settlements of economic hedges;
•A $258 million increase to recover the costs and an authorized return, as applicable, associated with non-fuel riders;
•A $184 million increase associated with the 2025 Biennial Review;
•A $75 million increase in sales to electric utility retail customers, primarily due to an increase in cooling degree days;
•A $14 million increase in sales to electric utility retail customers associated with growth; and
•A $13 million increase in sales to electric utility retail customers associated with economic and other usage factors.
